    "original_positive_statement_preserved_verbatim": true,
    "numbered_argument_unchanged": true,
    "new_statement_refuted": "Assume Countable Choice, $L,\\epsilon_0>0$, and the periodic Coulomb-gauge Gauss equation of [[lem-qft-qed-coulomb-constraint]]. For every smooth periodic charge density $\\rho$ on $T_L^3$, there exists a smooth periodic potential $\\phi$ satisfying $-\\Delta\\phi=\\rho/\\epsilon_0$."
  },
